es.\n2. **Playing cards are visible and being used** — Cards are clearly visible in frames 1–3, 4–10, 20–22, and 28–30.\n3. **The action is on a stage/performance area** — All actions occur on a stage with a black table, blue curtain backdrop, and studio lighting.\n4. **The setting is a formal performance environment (TV studio/theater)** — The setting is unmistakably “The Tonight Show” studio, with hosts, band members, and audience reactions.\n5. **Multiple people are watching** — Jimmy Fallon, Questlove, and other members of The Roots are present and reacting in frames 4–14, 15–26, and 28–30.\n6. **Cards are being manipulated magically** — Cards are shuffled, selected, vanished, and reappeared in ways that suggest illusion (e.g., cards falling from the air, sudden appearances).\n\n---\n\n**Identification of Distinct Tricks:**\n\nWe identify **two distinct card tricks** based on clear temporal gaps, different routines, and transitions:\n\n---\n\n**Trick 1: Card Selection & Table Manipulation (Frames 1–14)**\n\n- **Frames 1–3:** Close-up of David Blaine handling cards on the table — shuffling and manipulating.\n- **Frames 4–10:** Wider shot showing Blaine performing for Jimmy Fallon and The Roots. Cards are on the table, and Blaine is interacting with them while others watch intently.\n- **Frames 11–14:** Reaction shots and conclusion of the trick — Fallon reacts with surprise and walks away, indicating the trick has ended.\n- **Verification:** All 6 criteria are met. This is a complete card trick performed on stage.\n\n---\n\n**Trick 2: Card Vanish & Rain of Cards (Frames 15–30)**\n\n- **Frames 15–19:** Setup phase — Blaine is not yet manipulating cards, but the group is gathered around the table.\n- **Frames 20–22:** Blaine holds up a card, then gestures — cards suddenly fall from the air around him and the others. This is a clear magical effect.\n- **Frames 23–26:** Reactions and reset — the trick appears to be concluded.\n- **Frames 28–30:** Cards are now scattered on the floor, and Blaine gestures toward them — possibly a follow-up or reveal, but the core magical moment (the card rain) has already occurred.\n- **Verification:** All 6 criteria are met. The vanishing and raining of cards constitutes a separate, complete magical routine.\n\n---\n\n**Why Not More?**\n\n- **No other distinct tricks** are visible in the remaining frames. Frames 15–19 are transitional or setup. Frame 27 is a reaction shot without card manipulation.\n- The two tricks are separated by a clear shift in action: the first involves table-based manipulation and selection; the second involves a dramatic, airborne card effect.\n- No partial tricks or off-stage moments are counted.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Final Count: 2 distinct magic tricks with playing cards performed on stage.**'}, {'batch_start': 180, 'batch_end': 210, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0582.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0583.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0584.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0585.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0586.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0587.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0588.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_0589.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1039.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1040.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1041.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1042.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1043.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1044.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1045.jpg', '/mnt/ss