lysis of the 30 provided frames, here is the evaluation for counting distinct magic tricks with playing cards performed on stage:\n\n---\n\n**Criteria Review:**\n\n1. **A person is performing a magic trick** — David Blaine is clearly the performer in all relevant frames.\n2. **Playing cards are visible and being used** — Cards are visible in multiple frames (e.g., Frames 1–4, 12–17, 18–20).\n3. **The action is on a stage/performance area** — All scenes occur on the “Tonight Show” or “SNL” stage, with visible studio lighting, curtains, and audience seating.\n4. **The setting is a formal performance environment (TV studio/theater)** — Confirmed by the studio sets, city skyline backdrop, and presence of hosts/guests.\n5. **Multiple people are watching** — Jimmy Fallon, Questlove, Priyanka Chopra, and others are present and observing.\n6. **Cards are being manipulated magically** — David Blaine is seen handling cards in ways that suggest sleight of hand or illusion (e.g., holding a card between fingers, fanning, or making it appear/disappear).\n\n---\n\n**Trick Identification:**\n\nWe must identify **distinct** tricks based on **temporal gaps**, **different routines**, or **clear transitions**.\n\n---\n\n### **Trick 1: Card Reveal with Jimmy Fallon (Frames 1–4)**\n\n- **Description**: David Blaine holds a single card (appears to be the Ace of Spades) between his fingers while Jimmy Fallon looks on closely. The card is presented as if it’s being magically revealed or controlled.\n- **Verification**: All 6 criteria are met. Cards are visible, manipulated, and the setting is formal with multiple observers.\n- **Status**: ✅ Valid distinct card trick.\n\n---\n\n### **Trick 2: Card Routine with Priyanka Chopra (Frames 5–17)**\n\n- **Description**: David Blaine performs a card trick involving Priyanka Chopra. He holds a deck, fans it, and appears to have her select or interact with a card. Jimmy Fallon is also involved, holding a card at one point. The routine involves multiple steps: fanning, selection, and revelation.\n- **Verification**: All 6 criteria met. Clear card manipulation, stage setting, multiple observers (including Questlove), and a sustained routine.\n- **Status**: ✅ Valid distinct card trick.\n\n---\n\n### **Trick 3: Card Trick Involving Questlove (Frames 18–30)**\n\n- **Description**: Questlove is now directly involved. He holds a card and appears to place it into David Blaine’s mouth (or vice versa — Blaine is holding a card near his mouth, and Questlove is manipulating it). This appears to be a separate, more physical card trick involving a prop (possibly a card being “eaten” or “transferred”).\n- **Verification**: Cards are visible (e.g., Frame 18, 20). The action is magical (card near mouth, apparent transfer). Setting is formal, multiple people watching (Fallon, Chopra, Questlove). This is a different routine from the previous two — involving a different participant and a different type of manipulation (oral/physical transfer vs. fanning/reveal).\n- **Status**: ✅ Valid distinct card trick.\n\n---\n\n**Note on Transitions:**\n\n- There is a clear visual and contextual transition between Trick 1 (Frames 1–4) and Trick 2 (Frames 5–17) — the camera pulls back, new participants enter, and the routine changes.\n- Trick 3 (Frames 18–30) begins with a new interaction involving Questlove and a different card handling method, clearly distinct from the prior tricks.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\n✅ **Total Count of Distinct Card Magic Tricks Performed on Stage: 3**\n\n---'}, {'batch_start': 240, 'batch_end': 270, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1150.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1151.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1152.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1153.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/k2FIFQIYBvA/frames/frame_1154.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/vide